ICC color profiles are binary files that cannot be represented as text.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
 🎨  ASH DOTFILES v5.0 — DISPLAY P3 COLOR PROFILE SETUP
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Download the Display P3 ICC profile from:

  ICC registry (Display P3, Apple):
  https://registry.color.org/rgb-registry/displayp3

  Or extract from a macOS system:
  /System/Library/ColorSync/Profiles/Display P3.icc

Place the binary file at:
  ~/.config/color-profiles/Display-P3.icc

Then assign via:
  colormgr — GNOME/KDE color management daemon
  hyprland: monitor color_profile = ~/.config/color-profiles/Display-P3.icc

ASH integration:
  ash theme colors --profile Display-P3